# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Neural music generation — ACE-Step 1.5 (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Resonant Studio works with none of this set. The offline procedural engine
# composes and sings in the browser tab, and the neural engine simply shows
# "Not Connected" until a backend answers.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing here is required to be your own paths — every value has a default.

# Which neural backend the studio talks to:
#   local    an ACE-Step server you run yourself (the default; see below)
#   zerogpu  the ACE-Step Space on Hugging Face ZeroGPU — what the public site uses
ACE_STEP_BACKEND=local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ZeroGPU backend (ACE_STEP_BACKEND=zerogpu)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Space's own host, not its huggingface.co page. No token belongs here: the
# visitor's own Hugging Face sign-in is what authorises a generation, and a
# token in this file would be baked into a public bundle.
# ACE_STEP_SPACE_URL=https://<owner>-<space>.hf.space

# Optional: pin the length, in seconds, that "Auto" becomes. Unset — the
# default — Auto sends no length and ACE-Step picks one from the lyric sheet,
# which is what keeps a long sheet from being cut off at a fixed budget. Set
# this only to override that with a fixed length.
# ACE_STEP_SPACE_AUTO_DURATION=

# Optional ceiling: longer requests are refused before anything is sent. Unset
# means no ceiling is claimed — not that every length fits the Space's GPU time.
# ACE_STEP_SPACE_MAX_DURATION=

# How long one generation may take, queue and cold start included.
# ACE_STEP_SPACE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=900

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local backend (ACE_STEP_BACKEND=local)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the ACE-Step API is listening. Matches ACE-Step's own default.
ACE_STEP_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001

# Which checkpoints to ask for. The first real test uses these two:
# the turbo DiT ships in the main model bundle; the 0.6B LM is a separate
# sub-model and the setup script downloads it explicitly.
ACE_STEP_MODEL=acestep-v15-turbo
ACE_STEP_LM_MODEL=acestep-5Hz-lm-0.6B

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where things live on disk (used by scripts/*-ace-step-macos.sh)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The ACE-Step source checkout.
ACE_STEP_HOME=~/Applications/ACE-Step-1.5

# The model weights, kept outside both repositories: they are ~10 GB, they are
# not source, and a separate directory means re-cloning ACE-Step never
# re-downloads them. Exported to ACE-Step as ACESTEP_CHECKPOINTS_DIR.
ACE_STEP_MODELS=~/Models/ACE-Step-1.5

# Host and port the backend binds. ACE_STEP_API_URL is derived from these when
# it is not set explicitly.
ACE_STEP_HOST=127.0.0.1
ACE_STEP_PORT=8001

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The browser bundle
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing to set. Vite only exposes VITE_-prefixed variables to the browser, so
# vite.config.ts reads this file with loadEnv and bakes the ACE_STEP_* names
# above into the bundle at build time -- ACE_STEP_API_URL is enough for both
# the scripts and the app. Only those names are baked; nothing else in this
# file, a deploy token included, can reach the browser.
#
# The VITE_ forms below still work and take precedence, for anyone who would
# rather be explicit. They are overrides, not a second thing to remember.
# VITE_ACE_STEP_API_URL=
# VITE_ACE_STEP_MODEL=
# VITE_ACE_STEP_LM_MODEL=

# Only needed when the backend was started with ACESTEP_API_KEY set. A key in a
# browser bundle is a public key; put a real server in front for anything
# beyond your own machine.
# ACE_STEP_API_KEY=
# VITE_ACE_STEP_API_KEY=

# Because these are baked in at build time, changing one means rebuilding
# (npm run build) or restarting npm run dev.
#
# The full reference is docs/architecture/environment.md.

# --- signing in with Hugging Face --------------------------------------------
#
# The studio is private. A visitor who is not signed in sees a login page and
# nothing else — no tools, no offline engine, no application shell — and the
# Space refuses every request it cannot place, with 401 for no account and 403
# for the wrong one.
#
# Both values below are public: an OAuth *public client* has no secret, and the
# client id is sent to the browser by every OAuth flow there is. There is no
# client secret in this file, in the bundle, or anywhere in the frontend.
#
# The allowlist that decides who may actually GENERATE is not here — it lives in
# the Space as ALLOWED_HF_USERS, where the browser cannot read or change it.
#
# Unset VITE_HF_CLIENT_ID and there is no way into the application at all: the
# login page says signing in is not configured, which is the honest answer for
# a build that cannot sign anyone in.
# VITE_HF_CLIENT_ID=
#
# Who the login page admits, in the Space's own format: comma or space
# separated, matched case-insensitively. A username is public, so this is not a
# secret — and it is not the boundary either. It decides who is shown the
# application; the Space decides who may spend a GPU allowance, and it is the
# one that cannot be argued with from a browser. Unset means any account that
# signs in is shown the application.
# VITE_HF_ALLOWED_USERS=jamalbalya
#
# Optional. Defaults to https://huggingface.co.
# VITE_HF_PROVIDER_URL=
